#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-clock-o me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> Outside the daily window the profile simply stops applying, so the user regains normal access — it does not lock them out. An end earlier than the start spans midnight (22:00 → 06:00)."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-clock-o me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> This profile stops applying the moment the expiry passes, and the scheduled action archives it shortly after."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-exclamation-triangle me-2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Warning\" title=\"Warning\" /> <span> Nobody is targeted yet, so this profile does nothing. Add a <b>user</b> above, or a <b>group</b> to cover a whole role at once. </span>"
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-info-circle me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> <b>Invisible</b> also drops the field from export, search and group-by. A <b>Condition</b> is a Python expression on the record, e.g. <code>state == 'done'</code>. <b>Apply Field Domain</b> narrows what a relational field offers in its dropdown — it filters the picker, so pair it with a <b>Records</b> rule when the data must be genuinely out of reach."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-info-circle me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> <b>Invisible</b> also drops the field from list columns, search, group-by and server-side export. <b>Masked</b> shows it read-only with the value hidden (useful for salaries or IBANs). Leave <b>Condition</b> empty to apply always."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-info-circle me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> <b>Read-only</b> already blocks create, edit and delete on this model, server-side."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-info-circle me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> Everything here applies to <b>every model at once</b>, so you do not have to list them one by one. A switch set here cannot be re-enabled for a single model in the <b>Models</b> tab — restrict per model there instead when you need exceptions."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-info-circle me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> Hide a single header button, a notebook tab, a search filter or a group-by option. Turn on developer mode and hover an element to read its technical name — that name is the selector."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-info-circle me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> Leave this tab empty and the profile simply applies all the time. Set an expiry for temporary access (a contractor, an audit) — it stops applying the moment it passes and is auto-archived afterwards."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-info-circle me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> Menus are searched by their full path, so typing <b>Settings/Users</b> finds the right one straight away. Hiding a menu hides everything under it."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-info-circle me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> Notes are for administrators only — the restricted users never see them. Recording who asked for a profile is what makes an access review possible later."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-info-circle me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> One line per model. Use this to take away buttons (Create, Delete, Export...), whole view types, the chatter, or specific reports — enforced on the server, not just hidden in the interface."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-info-circle me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> Open a line to change what it restricts. Every switch here is enforced server-side, so it holds over XML-RPC and the API too."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-info-circle me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> Records <b>matching</b> a rule are the restricted ones. The rule name is what the user sees in the refusal message, so word it as the reason."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-info-circle me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> Restrict <b>which records</b> a person may touch — \"only their own orders\", \"nothing older than 30 days\". <b>Hide Only</b> makes a rule declutter the list without ever raising an error."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-info-circle me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> Selectors are technical names, not labels — turn on developer mode and hover an element to read its name. Notebook tabs also accept their visible label."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-info-circle me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> Sub-menus are hidden along with their parent. Hiding a menu does not block the data behind it — use <b>Models</b> or <b>Records</b> for that."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-info-circle me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Info\" title=\"Info\" /> The user keeps their own records (and their team's, on the subordinates setting) and is restricted from everyone else's. No domain to write."
msgstr ""

#. module: access_manager_pro
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:access_manager_pro.access_profile_view_form
msgid "<i class=\"fa fa-shield me-1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Effect\" title=\"Effect\" />"
msgstr ""

